		<setting type="lsep" label="For Build Creators" />
		<!-- The steps first, so nobody shuts Kodi down half way (the user, 2026-10-16), then the button: bold, green,
		     'START', last in the tab, so it reads as the one thing to press, not one more line of the notes (the user,
		     2026-10-18: from across a living room it looked like a statement). Kodi's settings list cannot centre a row.
		     The notes are disabled rows: Kodi draws them in its own dim grey and the remote skips them, so START is the
		     only row that lights up (as the user saw, every note row took the highlight when they were plain labels). -->
		<setting type="text" label="Do this last, after any clean-up inside Kodi." enable="false" />
		<setting type="text" label="Press START below and answer its two questions." enable="false" />
		<setting type="text" label="Takes a minute or two. Please let the clean finish: Kodi force closes when done." enable="false" />
